   "source": [
    "# 🌱 PlantVillage Agricultural Computer Vision & Disease Diagnosis System\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction: Global Food Security and the Role of AI\n",
    "One of the greatest challenges of the 21st century is maintaining the delicate balance between meeting the nutritional needs of a rapidly growing global population and the sustainability of limited agricultural resources. Data from the **FAO (Food and Agriculture Organization)** indicates that plant diseases and pests cause an annual yield loss of **20% to 40%** in global agricultural production.\n",
    "\n",
    "This project utilizes the **PlantVillage dataset**, a benchmark in agricultural computer vision, to build an end-to-end Deep Learning pipeline. We leverage **Transfer Learning** with **MobileNetV2** architecture to create a lightweight, efficient, and high-accuracy disease detection system capable of identifying 38 different classes across 14 crop species."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1.1 Environment Setup & Library Imports\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import zipfile\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import splitfolders  # For splitting data into Train/Val/Test\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.applications import MobileNetV2\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras import layers, models, callbacks\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check hardware acceleration\n",
    "print(f\"TensorFlow Version: {tf.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(\"GPU Available:\" if tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU') else \"GPU Not Available (Running on CPU)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Data Engineering: The PlantVillage Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset consists of **54,303 healthy and unhealthy leaf images** divided into 38 categories by species and disease. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Strategy\n",
    "1. **Ingestion:** Loading raw images from the source.\n",
    "2. **Splitting:** To prevent *Data Leakage*, we physically split the dataset into:\n",
    "   - **Train (80%):** For updating model weights.\n",
    "   - **Validation (10%):** For hyperparameter tuning and preventing overfitting.\n",
    "   - **Test (10%):** For final unbiased evaluation.\n",
    "3. **Preprocessing:** Resizing to 224x224 pixels and normalizing pixel values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 2.1 Data Extraction and Splitting Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "# Note: The user is expected to place 'archive.zip' in the root directory.\n",
    "zip_path = \"archive.zip\"\n",
    "extract_path = \"data/raw\"\n",
    "processed_path = \"data/processed\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 1: Extract Zip\n",
    "if os.path.exists(zip_path):\n",
    "    if not os.path.exists(extract_path):\n",
    "        print(\"Extracting raw data...\")\n",
    "        with zipfile.ZipFile(zip_path, 'r') as zip_ref:\n",
    "            zip_ref.extractall(extract_path)\n",
    "        print(\"Extraction complete.\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Step 2: Split Data\n",
    "    # We assume the extracted folder is named 'PlantVillage'\n",
    "    input_folder = os.path.join(extract_path, \"PlantVillage\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not os.path.exists(processed_path):\n",
    "        print(\"Splitting data into Train/Val/Test ratios (80/10/10)...\")\n",
    "        splitfolders.ratio(input_folder, output=processed_path, \n",
    "                           seed=42, ratio=(.8, .1, .1), \n",
    "                           group_prefix=None, move=False)\n",
    "        print(\"Data splitting complete.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"Data already processed and split.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"WARNING: 'archive.zip' not found. Please upload the dataset to run the pipeline.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 2.2 Data Loading & Generators\n",
    "IMG_SIZE = (224, 224)\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 32\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(processed_path):\n",
    "    print(\"Loading datasets from disk...\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    train_ds = tf.keras.utils.image_dataset_from_directory(\n",
    "        os.path.join(processed_path, 'train'),\n",
    "        image_size=IMG_SIZE, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, label_mode='categorical', shuffle=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    val_ds = tf.keras.utils.image_dataset_from_directory(\n",
    "        os.path.join(processed_path, 'val'),\n",
    "        image_size=IMG_SIZE, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, label_mode='categorical', shuffle=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    test_ds = tf.keras.utils.image_dataset_from_directory(\n",
    "        os.path.join(processed_path, 'test'),\n",
    "        image_size=IMG_SIZE, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, label_mode='categorical', shuffle=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    class_names = train_ds.class_names\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nTotal Classes Identified: {len(class_names)}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Optimize I/O performance (Prefetching & Caching)\n",
    "    AUTOTUNE = tf.data.AUTOTUNE\n",
    "    train_ds = train_ds.cache().shuffle(1000).prefetch(buffer_size=AUTOTUNE)\n",
    "    val_ds = val_ds.cache().prefetch(buffer_size=AUTOTUNE)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Processed data not found. Run the extraction step first.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Model Architecture: Transfer Learning with MobileNetV2\n",
    "\n",
    "We utilize **MobileNetV2** as our backbone. This architecture is chosen for its **Depthwise Separable Convolutions** and **Inverted Residuals**, making it highly efficient for potential mobile deployment (Edge AI).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Methodology:\n",
    "1. **Feature Extraction:** We freeze the pre-trained weights (trained on ImageNet) of the MobileNetV2 base to retain low-level feature recognition (edges, textures).\n",
    "2. **Custom Head:** We add a Global Average Pooling layer, Dropout (for regularization), and a final Dense Softmax layer for our 38 classes.\n",
    "3. **Fine-Tuning:** (Optional in later stages) Unfreezing the top layers to adapt abstract features to specific plant disease patterns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 3.1 Model Construction\n",
    "\n",
    "# Data Augmentation layer to improve generalization\n",
    "data_augmentation = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
    "    layers.RandomFlip(\"horizontal\"),\n",
    "    layers.RandomRotation(0.2),\n",
    "    layers.RandomZoom(0.2),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_model():\n",
    "    # Load MobileNetV2 without the top classification layer\n",
    "    base_model = MobileNetV2(input_shape=IMG_SIZE + (3,), include_top=False, weights='imagenet')\n",
    "    base_model.trainable = False  # Freeze base layers\n",
    "\n",
    "    inputs = tf.keras.Input(shape=IMG_SIZE + (3,))\n",
    "    x = data_augmentation(inputs)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # MobileNetV2 expects input in [-1, 1]\n",
    "    x = tf.keras.applications.mobilenet_v2.preprocess_input(x)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    x = base_model(x, training=False)\n",
    "    x = layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D()(x)\n",
    "    x = layers.Dropout(0.2)(x)  # Reduce overfitting\n",
    "    outputs = layers.Dense(len(class_names), activation='softmax')(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "    model = models.Model(inputs, outputs)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    model.compile(optimizer='adam', \n",
    "                  loss='categorical_crossentropy', \n",
    "                  metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "    return model\n",
    "\n",
    "if 'class_names' in locals():\n",
    "    model = build_model()\n",
    "    model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 3.2 Training Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "# Callbacks for professional training management\n",
    "checkpoint = callbacks.ModelCheckpoint(\"best_model.keras\", save_best_only=True, monitor=\"val_loss\")\n",
    "early_stop = callbacks.EarlyStopping(monitor=\"val_loss\", patience=3, restore_best_weights=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "EPOCHS = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(processed_path):\n",
    "    print(\"Starting training loop...\")\n",
    "    history = model.fit(\n",
    "        train_ds,\n",
    "        validation_data=val_ds,\n",
    "        epochs=EPOCHS,\n",
    "        callbacks=[checkpoint, early_stop]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    print(\"Training complete.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4. Evaluation and Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "if 'history' in locals():\n",
    "    # Plotting Accuracy and Loss Curves\n",
    "    acc = history.history['accuracy']\n",
    "    val_acc = history.history['val_accuracy']\n",
    "    loss = history.history['loss']\n",
    "    val_loss = history.history['val_loss']\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "    plt.plot(acc, label='Training Accuracy')\n",
    "    plt.plot(val_acc, label='Validation Accuracy')\n",
    "    plt.title('Accuracy Analysis')\n",
    "    plt.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "    plt.plot(loss, label='Training Loss')\n",
    "    plt.plot(val_loss, label='Validation Loss')\n",
    "    plt.title('Loss Analysis')\n",
    "    plt.legend()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Conclusion and Future Work\n",
    "\n",
    "This project successfully implements a **Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)** capable of diagnosing plant diseases with high accuracy using Transfer Learning. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Future Improvements:\n",
    "1. **Object Detection:** Integrating YOLOv8 to detect multiple leaves in a single frame.\n",
    "2. **Edge Deployment:** Converting the model to TensorFlow Lite (.tflite) for offline mobile application usage.\n",
    "3. **Explainability (XAI):** Implementing Grad-CAM to visualize the specific leaf regions influencing the model's decision, increasing trust for agricultural experts."
   ]
  }
